# Patch1 edits a.c in place while patch2 copies a.c to b.c with no hunks. The
# copy is keyed by b.c, so nothing pairs. a.c must show patch1's edit with a
# note that the other patch copies the file to b.c, and b.c must show patch2's
# copy with a note that the other patch has text changes for the source a.c. A
# copy leaves its source untouched, so neither note claims that patch2 edits
# a.c.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
